  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Jatin Kumar vs State Of U.P. on 21 July, 2022 Author: Siddharth Bench: Siddharth High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Court No. - 76 Case :- Criminal Misc. Bail Application No. - 29356 of 2022 Applicant :- Jatin Kumar Opposite Party :- State of U.P. Counsel for Applicant :- Anil Kumar Singh,Akhilesh Kumar Vishwakarma Counsel for Opposite Party :- G.A. Hon'ble Siddharth,J.",
    "facts": "The instant bail application has been filed on behalf of the applicant, Jatin Kumar, with a prayer to release him on bail in Case Crime No. 77 of 2022, under Sections 272, 419, 420, 467, 468, 471 IPC & 60(1), 63/72 Excise Act, Police Station Rampur, District- Jaunpur, during pendency of trial. Offence under section 60(1), 63/72 of Excise Act is bailable and triable by Magistrate. False recovery has been alleged. The applicant is languishing in jail since 25.5.2022.",
    "arguments": "Per contra learned A.G.A. has opposed the prayer for bail of the applicant by contending that the innocence of the applicant cannot be adjudged at pre trial stage, therefore, he does not deserves any indulgence. In case the applicant is released on bail he will again indulge in similar activities and will misuse the liberty of bail. Having considered the submissions of the parties noted above, larger mandate of the Article 21 of the Constitution of India, Satendra Kumar Antil Vs. C.B.I. & Another, passed in S.L.P.(Crl.) No. 5191 of 2021, and without expressing any opinion on the merits of the case, let the applicant involved in the aforesaid crime be released on bail on his furnishing a personal bond and two sureties each in the like amount to the satisfaction of the court concerned with the following conditions that :- (i) The applicant shall not tamper with the evidence or threaten the witnesses. (ii) The applicant shall file an undertaking to the effect that he shall not seek any adjournment on the dates fixed for evidence when the witnesses are present in Court.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Per contra learned A.G.A. has opposed the prayer for bail of the applicant by contending that the innocence of the applicant cannot be adjudged at pre trial stage, therefore, he does not deserves any indulgence. In case the applicant is released on bail he will again indulge in similar activities and will misuse the liberty of bail.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "Having considered the submissions of the parties noted above, larger mandate of the Article 21 of the Constitution of India, Satendra Kumar Antil Vs. C.B.I. & Another, passed in S.L.P.(Crl.) No. 5191 of 2021, and without expressing any opinion on the merits of the case, let the applicant involved in the aforesaid crime be released on bail on his furnishing a personal bond and two sureties each in the like amount to the satisfaction of the court concerned with the following conditions that :- (i) The applicant shall not tamper with the evidence or threaten the witnesses. (ii) The applicant shall file an undertaking to the effect that he shall not seek any adjournment on the dates fixed for evidence when the witnesses are present in Court."
  },
